What kind of draft is that?

265
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:16,040
- Yeah, let's go.
- Chill.

266
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:18,000
Yeah, that's how it's done!

267
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:19,600
Set an ambush!

268
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:20,760
I'm low HP.

269
00:18:20,760 --> 00:18:21,920
I'm falling back.

270
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,960
- We can get this.
- Dive in.

271
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:25,920
Like that!

272
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,800
(Cannon Minion)

273
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:30,120
(The Blue Team's tower
has been destroyed)

274
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:34,320
- Dive in!
- Go for it!

275
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:37,800
Let the wave in.

276
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:40,920
Screw it.
They picked such a weird draft.

277
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:43,600
Push! Go for it!

278
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,400
We can finish this.

279
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:47,240
Exactly.

280
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:49,160
Then let's finish it!

281
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:50,960
Here we go!

282
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:52,720
The creeps are here.

283
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:06,680
- Bring it on!
- Confused, huh?

284
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:08,000
Getting confused, aren't you?

285
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:18,120
You can't touch me.

286
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:19,840
You're getting it, too.

287
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,560
A total fake-out right here.

288
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,240
Peem!

289
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,560
P'Jack, the bottom lane is open.

290
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:34,600
Come on.

291
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:36,280
You can do it. Dive it.

292
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:39,400
This is more like it.

293
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:42,680
Dive in.

294
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,640
Perfect.

295
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:47,600
Get the Dark Slayer.

296
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:53,680
Soh, you go first. I'll back you up.

297
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:57,960
Right now!

298
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:06,160
(Derya's got
the high ground towers down.)

299
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:07,440
(Is this game over?)

300
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,880
- Hey!
- Damn it.

301
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:15,000
What the f*ck are you guys doing?

302
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:18,480
They're totally lost.

303
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,560
You're just chickens, you know.

304
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:22,440
Two wins now, baby!

305
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:25,560
Guys, watch out.

306
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:28,160
Nice!

307
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:31,160
That was a beautiful play!

308
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:35,440
(It looks like
JJack is their target right now.)

309
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:37,320
Counter! Right now!

310
00:20:40,560 --> 00:20:41,840
This is it. Do it.

311
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:45,720
Nice!

312
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:47,560
Dive their Carry first!

313
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:55,160
He's running for his life.

314
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:57,600
You sure you got this, Peem?

315
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:58,760
This is actually working.

316
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:01,160
- Last hit! Do it, Laem!
- Last hit!

317
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:02,080
Push mid first.

318
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:07,160
Go, go, go.

319
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,360
Now that's time to dive in!

320
00:21:15,760 --> 00:21:16,640
Nice!

321
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:19,320
- Dive in!
- Dive in!

322
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:22,480
They're diving in.

323
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:23,960
Let's dive in.

324
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:25,200
We can counter.

325
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:26,600
- Here we go.
- That's nice.

326
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,800
Whoa, I should've played Support
in the first place.

327
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:38,240
What the f*ck are you doing?

328
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:42,440
(All that's left is
to clear the remaining towers.)

329
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:43,560
Dive in!

330
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:45,960
Go, go.

331
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,320
Let's go, guys.

332
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:50,360
- Nice!
- Push, push.

333
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:51,120
We got this.

334
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,480
We got this. Yes!

335
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:04,680
Three wins!

336
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:06,400
Take that, Blue Viper!

337
00:22:17,680 --> 00:22:18,840
Hey, I'm taking the Sage Buff!

338
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:21,360
- Take it. Here you go.
- Here I come!

339
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:24,840
Go, go!

340
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:27,000
Kill them all.

341
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,040
Guys, dive it.

342
00:22:28,240 --> 00:22:29,240
This is our chance.

343
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:31,040
Come on.

344
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:35,840
- Come on, this is it.
- Let's go!

345
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:40,480
I can get more kills.

346
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,120
That's how it's done!

347
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:02,240
(What a clean play from B.S. Brothers!)

348
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:06,160
(They secured the kills.
What a play!)

349
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:09,280
(They took the bottom tower, too!)

350
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:13,560
Let's make sure we take this final round.

351
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:15,960
- Sh*t, we're losing!
- They're all ganking us!

352
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:22,120
- Come on, the top lane.
- Let's go.

353
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:25,760
Nice, Soh!

354
00:23:26,120 --> 00:23:27,120
You better be ready.

355
00:23:27,240 --> 00:23:28,280
Dive in.

356
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:29,240
Dive in now.

357
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:32,160
Let's go. Diving in.

358
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:33,800
Nice!

359
00:23:35,360 --> 00:23:36,680
That was nice, Soh!

360
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:39,320
Push! Push now.

361
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:51,000
Careful! Someone's hiding in the bush!

362
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:54,080
Checked. All clear.

363
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:56,120
No one there. Already checked.

364
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:57,240
Guys, I can't hold them off!

365
00:23:57,280 --> 00:23:59,280
- Go, go, push!
- Finish them!

366
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:02,840
(With the creeps pushing in,
can B.S. Brothers finish the game?)

367
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:06,080
- Go for it! Dive in!
- Here we go!

368
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:09,600
Dive in now.

369
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:23,920
Dammit!

370
00:24:39,800 --> 00:24:40,760
Jeez.

371
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:53,400
F*ck, what the hell was that play?

372
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:55,800
We did it, Soh! We actually did it!

373
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:57,640
B.S. Brothers!

374
00:24:57,680 --> 00:25:05,520
- B.S. Brothers! B.S. Brothers!
- B.S. Brothers! B.S. Brothers!

375
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:06,720
That means...

376
00:25:06,840 --> 00:25:08,840
- B.S. Brothers,
- B.S. Brothers,

377
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:11,920
- you are the APL 2026 Champions!
- you are the APL 2026 Champions!

378
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:15,000
♪Birthday but with me♪

379
00:25:15,040 --> 00:25:17,720
(B.S. Brothers!)

380
00:25:18,840 --> 00:25:20,240
(Congratulations!)

381
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:22,120
(Incredible!)

382
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:24,520
♪Could it be I'm missing you?♪

383
00:25:26,760 --> 00:25:28,600
Look at this! Check it out!

384
00:25:32,720 --> 00:25:33,880
Let me try!

385
00:25:33,920 --> 00:25:37,480
♪The more it happens, the more I see♪

386
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:40,480
♪Yeah, it must be♪

387
00:25:43,360 --> 00:25:44,320
Go for it, Jack!

388
00:25:44,360 --> 00:25:46,600
Man, I'm on fire!

389
00:25:50,520 --> 00:25:51,680
Your turn!

390
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:53,440
One, two...

391
00:25:58,680 --> 00:26:00,000
- Do it!
- Go, P'Toobtub!

392
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:15,360
(The player who stepped in
when the team needed them most)

393
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:19,400
(and perfectly shifted
the momentum of the game,)

394
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:24,600
or the FMVP of this tournament, is...

395
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:31,560
The FMVP is...

396
00:26:31,560 --> 00:26:33,320
- It's you, P'Three.
- Derya!

397
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:42,280
MVP!

398
00:26:42,360 --> 00:26:46,360
- MVP!
- MVP!

399
00:26:47,960 --> 00:26:49,480
Hey, give us a smile.

400
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:52,480
You deserve this more than anyone.

401
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:54,040
Not just on this stage,

402
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:55,880
but from the moment
you joined our team...

403
00:26:56,120 --> 00:26:57,760
and entered my life,

404
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,480
you've been my MVP.

405
00:27:01,360 --> 00:27:03,200
You've been my MVP, too.

406
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:08,000
- Someone's so in love here.
- Is it time yet?

407
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,160
- Ready?
- Go for it!

408
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:11,400
- Alright, group photo!
- Yeah, come on!

409
00:27:11,440 --> 00:27:13,080
- Jeez, what's with you?
- Get in the shot!

410
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:15,080
Jeez.

411
00:27:15,560 --> 00:27:17,680
Where's the camera? Bring it here!

412
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:19,680
One, two, three!

413
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:22,720
- B.S. Brothers!
- B.S. Brothers!

414
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:41,640
And we actually made it happen.

415
00:27:48,920 --> 00:27:50,240
I never imagined...

416
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:53,920
that I would actually
win this FMVP award.

417
00:27:54,680 --> 00:27:56,520
I honestly thought P'Three would get it.

418
00:27:58,560 --> 00:28:00,840
Anyway, thank you, everyone...

419
00:28:01,440 --> 00:28:04,280
for always supporting me.

420
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:06,600
At first, I thought...

421
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:10,040
I'd only be taking
this FMVP trophy home.

422
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:12,200
But actually, it's much more than that.

423
00:28:13,040 --> 00:28:13,960
Right now,

424
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:17,640
RoV has given me
the opportunity to design a skin.

425
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:22,280
That's my biggest problem

426
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:23,640
because I still have no idea...

427
00:28:23,680 --> 00:28:26,680
how I'm going to design my own skin.

428
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:31,560
If it's not too much trouble,
could you help me out?

429
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:39,560
If you have any ideas,
please let me know.

430
00:28:47,880 --> 00:28:50,120
Derya,

431
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:52,600
your babe is home!

432
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:55,120
I've been gone all day. So exhausted.

433
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:01,920
Whoa, what's all this?

434
00:29:06,520 --> 00:29:08,920
A strict art professor
wouldn't approve of this.

435
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:10,600
Soh?

436
00:29:11,960 --> 00:29:13,000
Where are you?

437
00:29:16,080 --> 00:29:16,840
Soh!

438
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:18,600
- P'Three...
- Whoa!

439
00:29:19,280 --> 00:29:21,360
Soh, where are you?

440
00:29:21,840 --> 00:29:23,160
P'Three...

441
00:29:24,760 --> 00:29:26,640
P'Three...

442
00:29:29,160 --> 00:29:30,560
A ghost!

443
00:29:32,160 --> 00:29:33,680
Soh, Soh!

444
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:42,240
How could I not be startled?

445
00:29:42,240 --> 00:29:45,000
I just finished
watching 'After Dark' on WeTV.

446
00:29:45,120 --> 00:29:47,000
Man, no wonder I was creeped out.

447
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:48,840
Come on, P'Three.

448
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:51,800
Did I really look
that much like a ghost?

449
00:29:52,880 --> 00:29:54,280
Don't be silly.

450
00:29:58,000 --> 00:29:59,880
Even if you were a ghost,

451
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:01,880
you'd be my only boo.

452
00:30:02,360 --> 00:30:04,280
You know, my one and only boo.

453
00:30:05,040 --> 00:30:05,720
Stop right there.

454
00:30:05,760 --> 00:30:08,320
I heard someone screamed
really loud just now.

455
00:30:10,320 --> 00:30:11,120
Wonder who that could be.

456
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:14,200
I'm sorry.

457
00:30:14,400 --> 00:30:17,160
I only went home
to help out for a little bit.

458
00:30:17,240 --> 00:30:20,440
Now that I'm back,
why is my boyfriend like this?

459
00:30:20,840 --> 00:30:23,480
I left you alone for just a second.

460
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:26,320
Whoa, I really can't
let you out of my sight.

461
00:30:27,360 --> 00:30:28,240
Soh,

462
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:30,720
you need to take care of yourself, okay?

463
00:30:31,440 --> 00:30:33,240
You're the only one for me
in this world.

464
00:30:36,080 --> 00:30:37,040
So...

465
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:40,480
can I ask you for a favor?

466
00:30:40,520 --> 00:30:42,800
Of course. Whatever you want me to do,

467
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:44,400
just name it.
I'll do anything for you.

468
00:30:50,040 --> 00:30:54,200
Then, could you help me design the skin?

469
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:58,680
Oh, come on, is that all?
I've totally got this.

470
00:30:58,800 --> 00:30:59,920
Did that hurt?

471
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:01,240
It didn't.

472
00:31:01,440 --> 00:31:02,000
Okay...

473
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:06,800
It's not quite 100% done.

474
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:12,240
Why is designing a skin so damn hard?

475
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:19,480
But out of all of these,
I really like this one.

476
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:21,240
This one, the lion skin.

477
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:24,120
It looks like
a fierce, imposing predator, like...

478
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:26,360
That's a cat.

479
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:33,440
Do you have your favorite one yet?

480
00:31:37,960 --> 00:31:39,400
It's okay.

481
00:31:39,800 --> 00:31:41,880
We'll keep trying, okay?

482
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:47,560
What do you want people to see
in this skin?

483
00:31:50,080 --> 00:31:51,400
I don't really know.

484
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:57,560
Maybe a side of me
that others haven't seen before.

485
00:31:58,240 --> 00:31:59,480
A side of you?

486
00:32:01,480 --> 00:32:04,360
People usually see me as a derpy kid,

487
00:32:04,400 --> 00:32:05,320
a nerd,

488
00:32:05,680 --> 00:32:06,640
or just a plain guy.

489
00:32:08,160 --> 00:32:10,120
I just want to explore a new side of me,

490
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:14,320
in case it works for the skin.

491
00:32:18,320 --> 00:32:20,360
Don't you worry, Derpy Kid.

492
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:23,960
I'm going to help you find that side.

493
00:32:28,920 --> 00:32:29,600
Come on.

494
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:33,000
Let's find your ultimate skin, baby.

495
00:32:40,680 --> 00:32:42,880
I think you need to try something new.

496
00:32:51,160 --> 00:32:52,040
A Luk Thung singer?

497
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:55,280
Exactly. This is something
totally different for you.

498
00:32:55,320 --> 00:32:56,640
Luk Thung music...

499
00:32:56,680 --> 00:33:01,200
will definitely reveal
another side of you for sure.

500
00:33:01,440 --> 00:33:03,200
Trust me, Derpy Kid.

501
00:33:03,240 --> 00:33:04,800
♪Alright, baby?♪

502
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:06,800
- ♪Alright, baby?♪
- ♪Alright, baby?♪

503
00:33:17,360 --> 00:33:18,200
Gosh!

504
00:33:19,160 --> 00:33:20,080
P'Three!

505
00:33:20,520 --> 00:33:21,960
- What?
- Is this my new side,

506
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:23,800
or is it actually yours?

507
00:33:23,840 --> 00:33:25,040
Since Luk Thung didn't work,

508
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:26,680
I think you need a spiritual retreat.

509
00:33:27,360 --> 00:33:28,040
Alright.

510
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:32,800
Master Three...

511
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:37,280
I think...

512
00:33:37,560 --> 00:33:39,120
that one was a bit too chaotic.

513
00:33:39,800 --> 00:33:40,840
For you,

514
00:33:40,840 --> 00:33:44,160
something quiet and peaceful
might be better.

515
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:48,720
Let's meditate.

516
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:53,280
A peaceful mind...

517
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:55,880
brings clarity.

518
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:57,320
When there's clarity,

519
00:33:57,760 --> 00:33:59,520
the answers reveal themselves.

520
00:34:05,480 --> 00:34:06,920
Jeez, P'Three.

521
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:10,000
I think this is too peaceful.

522
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:12,000
- And I'm itchy.
- It's not working?

523
00:34:12,360 --> 00:34:13,440
I don't think it is.

524
00:34:13,480 --> 00:34:14,880
Then let's try something else.

525
00:34:15,160 --> 00:34:16,200
Let's try something else.

526
00:34:18,280 --> 00:34:19,560
Hey, Soh!

527
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:22,640
What's going on here?

528
00:34:22,680 --> 00:34:24,280
Trouble finds me every time.

529
00:34:24,440 --> 00:34:25,760
Scientists have said that...

530
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:27,960
if we're in a thrilling situation,

531
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,240
the adrenaline will start flowing

532
00:34:29,280 --> 00:34:31,200
and help us discover our hidden skills.

533
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:33,400
How are you doing?

534
00:34:33,400 --> 00:34:34,680
Found any new sides of yourself?

535
00:34:34,680 --> 00:34:36,040
Isn't this a bit too thrilling?

536
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:37,720
What now?

537
00:34:42,600 --> 00:34:44,360
How's it going? Any new ideas?

538
00:34:45,520 --> 00:34:47,800
My ideas were blown away
by that first explosion.

539
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:49,640
Jeez, really? Nothing at all?

540
00:34:55,720 --> 00:34:56,920
Listen, Derpy Kid.

541
00:34:56,920 --> 00:34:59,000
I think we should try
a film noir vibe.

542
00:34:59,040 --> 00:35:00,720
Whoa, I think this is better.

543
00:35:00,720 --> 00:35:02,240
- This is the one.
- That's enough, P'Three.

544
00:35:03,240 --> 00:35:04,160
I think...

545
00:35:04,360 --> 00:35:06,400
I've explored plenty of new sides now,

546
00:35:08,080 --> 00:35:10,040
but none of them actually felt like me.

547
00:35:10,600 --> 00:35:14,560
Maybe I'm just a plain, ordinary guy

548
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:17,760
with nothing special.

549
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:21,560
Oh, Soh.

550
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:23,640
Don't put so much pressure on yourself.

551
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:25,440
Let's just take our time.

552
00:35:26,040 --> 00:35:26,800
Okay?

553
00:35:30,120 --> 00:35:31,400
No matter what you're like,

554
00:35:31,920 --> 00:35:34,480
you'll always have me
as your number one support.

555
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:43,200
I've got it.

556
00:35:43,680 --> 00:35:45,520
I have one more thing I want you to try.

557
00:35:46,480 --> 00:35:47,280
What is it?

558
00:35:48,440 --> 00:35:49,480
Just a second.

559
00:35:58,080 --> 00:35:59,360
Here.

560
00:36:01,120 --> 00:36:03,560
Wait, that's my bear head.

561
00:36:04,320 --> 00:36:05,720
I thought I'd lost it.

562
00:36:06,880 --> 00:36:10,200
Oh, your fans made this one for you.

563
00:36:10,240 --> 00:36:11,680
- My fans?
- Yeah.

564
00:36:12,360 --> 00:36:13,920
But why did they send it to you?

565
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:19,560
Look at you, catching on.

566
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:22,280
I was planning to keep it
as a little secret.

567
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:23,680
I wanted all the credit for myself.

568
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:25,560
I'll admit it.

569
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:26,520
This...

570
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:28,480
Your boyfriend made it himself.

571
00:36:31,760 --> 00:36:34,360
I know how much this means to you.

572
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:37,360
It's a part of who you are.

573
00:36:37,920 --> 00:36:39,400
I couldn't just let it disappear.

574
00:36:52,640 --> 00:36:53,720
Because...

575
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:06,000
you're already
the most important person in my life.

576
00:37:37,520 --> 00:37:45,240
♪They say the words we cannot say
are hidden in songs we play,♪

577
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:52,240
♪So I'm sending you this one,
hoping you'll feel the same way♪

578
00:37:52,880 --> 00:37:56,920
♪And hear what my heart's
been trying to say♪

579
00:37:56,960 --> 00:38:02,920
♪It's that smile of yours
that gets me every time,♪

580
00:38:02,920 --> 00:38:10,600
♪Those eyes and that sweet smile,
they make my heart go wild♪

581
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:17,920
♪I'll give you my heart
if you ever need someone by your side♪

582
00:38:17,960 --> 00:38:20,080
♪(Just give me a sign)♪

583
00:38:20,560 --> 00:38:24,960
♪No matter how far,
I'll always come to you♪

584
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:30,680
♪I'll fill your heart with love
as long as you keep smiling, too♪

585
00:38:31,240 --> 00:38:35,640
♪When your tears start to fall,
I'll hold you tight♪

586
00:38:35,640 --> 00:38:41,600
♪And like a game, no matter how hard,
we'll win every fight♪

587
00:39:29,480 --> 00:39:30,960
It's as cute
as the person who designed it.

588
00:39:39,120 --> 00:39:41,760
Hello! Can I interview you guys
for a moment?

589
00:39:41,840 --> 00:39:42,560
Of course.

590
00:39:42,560 --> 00:39:45,600
Since you guys are out
jogging together like this,

591
00:39:45,640 --> 00:39:46,720
what's your relationship?

592
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:50,400
We're boyfriends.

593
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:59,160
♪I'll find my way
into your heart one day,♪

594
00:39:59,160 --> 00:40:01,720
♪Getting a little closer every day,♪

595
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:04,520
♪Before you even look my way,♪

596
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:09,520
♪Before you realize I'm here to stay♪

597
00:40:09,520 --> 00:40:12,760
♪For now,
I'll just keep things brotherly♪

598
00:40:12,800 --> 00:40:15,200
♪While caring for you secretly♪

599
00:40:15,240 --> 00:40:18,400
♪I'll leave no signs for you to see♪

600
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:25,560
♪Until your heart makes room for me♪

601
00:40:30,640 --> 00:40:31,640
Alright, then.

602
00:40:31,680 --> 00:40:33,760
- Can I take another photo with you?
- Of course.

603
00:40:33,760 --> 00:40:34,400
Come on.

604
00:40:34,440 --> 00:40:35,560
- Let's do a peace sign?
- Got it.

605
00:40:36,840 --> 00:40:37,840
Now, a heart.

606
00:40:39,960 --> 00:40:41,480
- Okay, thank you!
- Thank you!

607
00:40:45,040 --> 00:40:46,800
Soh is here!

608
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:08,680
Hello, ma boy.

609
00:41:13,040 --> 00:41:13,880
How...

610
00:41:15,480 --> 00:41:17,240
How do I look, P'Three?

611
00:41:18,600 --> 00:41:20,400
You look exactly like
the perfect boyfriend for me.

612
00:41:24,960 --> 00:41:26,000
Are you ready?

613
00:41:28,200 --> 00:41:29,080
- Ready?
- I'm ready.

614
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:30,880
I'm ready.

615
00:41:30,880 --> 00:41:32,120
- Good.
- Right now,

616
00:41:32,160 --> 00:41:37,000
we are at the launch event
for the new skin.

617
00:41:37,680 --> 00:41:38,920
Pardon me.

618
00:41:39,040 --> 00:41:42,360
Soh, can I get a quick interview?

619
00:41:42,440 --> 00:41:43,240
Sure.

620
00:41:44,040 --> 00:41:46,240
Is there anything
you'd like to say to your fans?

621
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:49,880
Hi, I'm Soh.

622
00:41:50,440 --> 00:41:53,800
I'm not sure
if you'll like the skin I designed.

623
00:41:54,160 --> 00:41:55,960
What do you think of it?
Have you seen it yet?

624
00:41:55,960 --> 00:41:57,960
Oh, the fans are asking...

625
00:41:57,960 --> 00:42:01,440
if that's Three over there.

626
00:42:02,360 --> 00:42:05,560
No need to turn away!
Look over here, come on.

627
00:42:09,640 --> 00:42:12,440
That's right, it's me,
Thr33Gamer, the one and only.

628
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:14,280
Thanks for still remembering me.

629
00:42:14,960 --> 00:42:19,000
But honestly, I feel like
I'm stealing the spotlight.

630
00:42:19,440 --> 00:42:22,640
P'Three actually helped me
design the skin.

631
00:42:23,440 --> 00:42:24,920
Without him,

632
00:42:25,480 --> 00:42:27,240
the skin wouldn't have
turned out this cute.

633
00:42:28,960 --> 00:42:30,440
The fans are screaming!

634
00:42:30,480 --> 00:42:31,400
But moving on,

635
00:42:31,440 --> 00:42:35,240
we'd love to know
the backstory of this skin

636
00:42:35,280 --> 00:42:38,640
that's going on sale
in just a few minutes.

637
00:42:38,640 --> 00:42:40,520
Could you explain it to us?

638
00:42:40,640 --> 00:42:41,480
Of course.

639
00:42:43,280 --> 00:42:44,480
For me,

640
00:42:45,120 --> 00:42:47,920
this skin represents memories.

641
00:42:48,880 --> 00:42:51,720
The wonderful memories that P'Three

642
00:42:52,360 --> 00:42:55,200
and everyone else on the team
gave to me.

643
00:42:55,600 --> 00:42:58,000
I wanted to pass them on to all of you.

644
00:43:01,520 --> 00:43:03,760
- (Get over here! A weapon, huh?)
- (Bring it on! Come on!)

645
00:43:05,520 --> 00:43:06,680
(No! Stop...)

646
00:43:07,800 --> 00:43:08,920
(Guys, cheers!)

647
00:43:10,240 --> 00:43:11,560
A Support player...

648
00:43:11,560 --> 00:43:12,480
(That was satisfying!)

649
00:43:12,480 --> 00:43:14,720
- Makes teammates feel secure,
- (Soh, I grilled this just for you.)

650
00:43:14,760 --> 00:43:16,760
- knowing they're not fighting alone.
- (Chicken breast is good for you.)

651
00:43:17,360 --> 00:43:18,520
But outside the game,

652
00:43:18,840 --> 00:43:20,600
it's actually my teammates and the fans

653
00:43:20,840 --> 00:43:22,480
who make me feel that way.

654
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:29,920
(Don't be stressed, Derpy Kid.)

655
00:43:38,640 --> 00:43:40,600
- (Hey, Soh! Put it in!)
- (Let's go!)

656
00:43:40,600 --> 00:43:44,240
(Pluck all this, take the championship!)

657
00:43:45,800 --> 00:43:46,960
(This is the prime tea tip!)

658
00:43:47,120 --> 00:43:49,040
So, from now on,

659
00:43:49,600 --> 00:43:53,600
let this little bear support
and fight alongside you.

660
00:43:55,280 --> 00:43:59,040
The fans are ready
to hit that buy button now.

661
00:43:59,080 --> 00:44:02,840
Is there anything
you'd like to say to the fans?

662
00:44:03,160 --> 00:44:05,280
If you have a soft spot
for this little bear, Derya,

663
00:44:06,200 --> 00:44:08,840
then let it support you all

664
00:44:08,880 --> 00:44:10,280
and fight by your side.

665
00:44:11,120 --> 00:44:13,920
Don't forget to top up your vouchers
and get your own little bear.

666
00:44:16,040 --> 00:44:18,840
What about you, Three?
Anything to say to the fans?

667
00:44:20,560 --> 00:44:22,720
Well, since Soh put it so nicely,

668
00:44:22,920 --> 00:44:25,120
please don't forget
to take this Derya bear

669
00:44:25,160 --> 00:44:26,480
to support you in your matches.

670
00:44:26,680 --> 00:44:28,000
However,

671
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:31,600
don't forget that
you can only own the skin

672
00:44:32,120 --> 00:44:35,520
because I'm the real owner
of this bear-head gamer's heart.

673
00:44:37,840 --> 00:44:38,880
How exciting!

674
00:44:39,440 --> 00:44:40,640
Give me a second to catch my breath.

675
00:44:41,000 --> 00:44:44,520
All of us here
are fans of B.S. Brothers.

676
00:45:07,680 --> 00:45:10,040
(P'Toobtub)

677
00:45:13,200 --> 00:45:13,920
Yes?

678
00:45:13,960 --> 00:45:15,400
(Get to the cafe!)

679
00:45:15,440 --> 00:45:16,240
(Right now!)

680
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:16,960
What?

681
00:45:21,000 --> 00:45:22,280
Is something wrong?

682
00:45:25,480 --> 00:45:27,440
- Why is it so quiet in here?
- Hey, P'Three! Soh!

683
00:45:28,520 --> 00:45:30,080
How did you guys get here?

684
00:45:30,240 --> 00:45:31,600
All of you are here?

685
00:45:34,560 --> 00:45:36,840
I missed this old vibe.

686
00:45:36,920 --> 00:45:39,040
The smell reminds me of my old home.

687
00:45:39,720 --> 00:45:42,320
Usually, "old home"
is code for a grave, you know.

688
00:45:43,760 --> 00:45:44,800
Watch your mouth!

689
00:45:47,000 --> 00:45:48,760
What did we agree on?

690
00:45:50,960 --> 00:45:53,080
Fine, I'll slap my mouth three times.

691
00:45:53,400 --> 00:45:57,080
Look at you.
Are you scared of your boyfriend now?

692
00:45:57,480 --> 00:45:58,480
Boyfriend, my *ss.

693
00:45:58,520 --> 00:46:00,080
Aw, come on.

694
00:46:01,000 --> 00:46:03,400
- Playing tough, huh?
- Guys, get over here!

695
00:46:03,480 --> 00:46:05,040
Hurry up, come in here.

696
00:46:07,680 --> 00:46:08,640
Come on!

697
00:46:10,920 --> 00:46:12,200
Easy there, sweetie.

698
00:46:12,720 --> 00:46:14,680
Stay calm now, my girl.

699
00:46:15,720 --> 00:46:16,920
Help me out!

700
00:46:17,400 --> 00:46:18,600
I haven't slept a wink.

701
00:46:18,640 --> 00:46:19,680
Tangran...

702
00:46:19,800 --> 00:46:22,880
has been crying from midnight till noon.

703
00:46:22,920 --> 00:46:23,760
I haven't had a single break.

704
00:46:23,800 --> 00:46:25,640
Help me babysit her, will you?

705
00:46:26,880 --> 00:46:27,680
Please.

706
00:46:29,680 --> 00:46:31,960
Soh, take her. Alright.

707
00:46:32,840 --> 00:46:33,680
Here, P'Three.

708
00:46:34,080 --> 00:46:35,160
Don't you want to hold her?

709
00:47:15,480 --> 00:47:18,000
- We were throwing hands right here.
- Shut up. Stop talking.

710
00:47:18,040 --> 00:47:19,800
Right, or I'll end up forgetting.

711
00:47:19,800 --> 00:47:23,680
- Yeah, you just keep blabbering on.
- Yeah, you're right.

712
00:47:24,280 --> 00:47:26,000
- Oh, there he is.
- Sit down.

713
00:47:26,000 --> 00:47:27,280
Your hair is a total mess.

714
00:47:27,480 --> 00:47:28,760
I'm beat. So exhausted.

715
00:47:28,800 --> 00:47:31,440
Getting my daughter, Tangran,
to go to sleep...

716
00:47:31,480 --> 00:47:33,120
She just wouldn't stop crying.

717
00:47:33,160 --> 00:47:34,720
So is she finally out?

718
00:47:34,800 --> 00:47:36,000
Just drifted off a second ago.

719
00:47:37,960 --> 00:47:40,600
But everything around here
has improved so much.

720
00:47:40,960 --> 00:47:42,560
It's nothing like
when I used to live here.

721
00:47:44,000 --> 00:47:45,960
I really have to thank you guys

722
00:47:46,040 --> 00:47:48,440
for putting this place on the map.

723
00:47:49,560 --> 00:47:52,120
Whoa, don't mention it.
It was a breeze.

724
00:47:52,160 --> 00:47:54,640
Your cafe is basically ours.

725
00:47:54,640 --> 00:47:56,960
Your kid is basically ours.

726
00:47:57,120 --> 00:48:00,200
- And your wife is basically...
- Our mother.

727
00:48:00,240 --> 00:48:01,600
Exactly.

728
00:48:03,200 --> 00:48:04,840
You've got a real big mouth, don't you?

729
00:48:06,040 --> 00:48:08,560
Come to think of it,
now that you guys aren't around...

730
00:48:08,640 --> 00:48:10,200
I miss you all like crazy.

731
00:48:10,400 --> 00:48:12,120
There's no one for me to annoy anymore.

732
00:48:13,520 --> 00:48:15,080
P'Laem is right.

733
00:48:15,440 --> 00:48:18,040
Ever since APL ended, we haven't
really been to the training camp.

734
00:48:18,760 --> 00:48:20,360
It's nice in a way, I guess,

735
00:48:21,120 --> 00:48:23,160
but it's also pretty lonely.

736
00:48:23,200 --> 00:48:23,960
Right.

737
00:48:24,720 --> 00:48:28,880
Ever since my daughter was born,
I haven't had a second to rest.

738
00:48:29,280 --> 00:48:31,800
I'm super busy
and barely getting any sleep.

739
00:48:34,440 --> 00:48:36,240
Anyway, what are you guys
up to these days?

740
00:48:36,920 --> 00:48:38,000
Well...

741
00:48:38,720 --> 00:48:40,840
I'm back to
being an office worker again,

742
00:48:41,840 --> 00:48:43,080
but on the bright side,

743
00:48:43,440 --> 00:48:45,000
the office is full of fans now.

744
00:48:45,880 --> 00:48:47,320
Jeez.

745
00:49:02,440 --> 00:49:05,120
You're my bias in B.S. Brothers!

746
00:49:05,240 --> 00:49:06,080
Thanks.

747
00:49:06,840 --> 00:49:08,320
Bye-bye!

748
00:49:11,760 --> 00:49:13,160
And one more thing...

749
00:49:13,440 --> 00:49:16,000
I have a new intern I need to train.

750
00:49:16,120 --> 00:49:17,520
You saw me waving at you earlier.

751
00:49:17,520 --> 00:49:19,080
Why didn't you bring me along?

752
00:49:20,920 --> 00:49:22,080
I knew it.

753
00:49:22,120 --> 00:49:23,160
Look at Laem.

754
00:49:23,200 --> 00:49:24,800
He looks like he's been in his final year
for three years.

755
00:49:25,080 --> 00:49:26,600
It's the damn company.

756
00:49:26,640 --> 00:49:29,000
They're working me to the bone.

757
00:49:29,000 --> 00:49:32,560
Meeting minutes,
coffee runs, photocopying...

758
00:49:32,600 --> 00:49:34,800
Man, they make me do everything.

759
00:49:34,840 --> 00:49:37,480
- It's always just me.
- Just you and you, huh?

760
00:49:37,520 --> 00:49:38,480
You're damn right.

761
00:49:38,600 --> 00:49:40,200
What the hell is this machine?

762
00:49:40,600 --> 00:49:43,320
They keep giving me work
I don't know how to do.

763
00:49:43,360 --> 00:49:44,880
Why are there so many buttons?

764
00:49:46,920 --> 00:49:48,240
God,

765
00:49:48,440 --> 00:49:50,560
could you please stop testing me?

766
00:49:50,600 --> 00:49:52,760
Send something good my way
for a change.

767
00:49:56,720 --> 00:49:58,240
- Boss?
- For you.

768
00:49:58,280 --> 00:50:00,320
I ordered the wrong thing.
I don't like whipped cream.

769
00:50:02,920 --> 00:50:04,960
- Oh, I feel so bad for you.
- Right?

770
00:50:04,960 --> 00:50:06,640
Yeah, I haven't seen you
stream live lately.

771
00:50:06,680 --> 00:50:09,440
Come on, you're acting like
you'd play with me if I streamed.

772
00:50:09,640 --> 00:50:11,800
You're so famous now, come on.

773
00:50:11,840 --> 00:50:13,960
No way, I'm not that famous.

774
00:50:13,960 --> 00:50:17,080
I'm just the breakout streamer
of the year, you know.

775
00:50:19,000 --> 00:50:20,640
That's it for now, everyone.

776
00:50:20,680 --> 00:50:24,480
How was that match?
Let me check the comments.

777
00:50:26,040 --> 00:50:28,080
(You look so cute today.)

778
00:50:28,200 --> 00:50:30,280
No way, you're kidding.

779
00:50:30,360 --> 00:50:31,640
Well said! I'll give you twenty.

780
00:50:31,680 --> 00:50:32,480
Wait!

781
00:50:33,120 --> 00:50:36,000
Did TenTen just donate ten thousand?

782
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:37,240
I'm so excited!

783
00:50:37,520 --> 00:50:39,000
Thank you!

784
00:50:39,760 --> 00:50:41,360
Not bad at all.

785
00:50:42,800 --> 00:50:44,720
I think you're more famous than me now.

786
00:50:44,760 --> 00:50:47,440
I could never compare
to the great Thr33Gamer.

787
00:50:47,880 --> 00:50:49,880
Just being able to come back
makes me so happy.

788
00:50:51,920 --> 00:50:52,960
So, how about you?

789
00:50:53,080 --> 00:50:54,520
Are you staying in Vietnam for long?

790
00:50:54,720 --> 00:50:56,800
Don't forget your old team
now that you've got a new one.

791
00:50:56,840 --> 00:50:58,160
You're always so dramatic.

792
00:50:58,320 --> 00:50:59,640
How could I ever forget you guys...

793
00:51:00,240 --> 00:51:01,760
when you're all this adorable?

794
00:51:01,800 --> 00:51:04,640
Wait, who's adorable? Tell me!

795
00:51:04,760 --> 00:51:05,800
Everyone, obviously.

796
00:51:06,040 --> 00:51:08,200
- Is that so?
- You sure?

797
00:51:08,360 --> 00:51:09,200
